data.reasoningText:
Found it! The page loads runs on mount **once** only:

```js
// Load run list on mount (once)
useEffect(() => {
  api
    .listRuns()
    .then((data) => setRuns(data))
    .finally(() => setLoadingRuns(false));
}, []);
```

Also, history is only fetched once per run:
```js
if (!histories[runId]) {
  api.getRunHistory(runId).then((h) => {
    setHistories((prev) => ({ ...prev, [runId]: h }));
  });
}
```

So the runs load once on mount and history gets cached per run with no polling. But the user said the run wasn't appearing at all—let me reconsider. The API is actually returning it correctly, so the issue was likely that the page loaded before the training process had written the `run_config.json` file.

Re-reading the session notes: the user restarted the server and the run still wasn't visible. Since the UI only fetches the run list once on mount, they'd need to refresh the page to see it. The API is now returning the run with 3 epochs, so the server is definitely serving it. I should check if training is still ongoing and whether the UI needs a polling mechanism to auto-refresh the run list.

